  "answer": "Project Zenith is a high-priority initiative aimed at driving innovation, optimizing cloud storage, and enhancing data analytics and visualization. Key milestones include a kick-off in Q3 2023 (with varying dates mentioned: June 15, July 15), a $500,000 budget for Phase One, and a subsequent executive-approved budget of $2M covering all phases. The project has seen progress in predictive analytics and AI integration, with a testing phase completed by October 10th. Leadership includes Sarah Tan, Marcus Cole, and Neil. Recent updates involve a compliance plan budget increase to $55,000, security protocol updates effective January next year, and a call for feedback on the prototype by the end of November. A detailed report on Phase Two progress is scheduled for the staff meeting on November 20th."
